me": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "3. When X began building its subway system (The Metro) for a 2004 event, they ran into a major problem: everywhere they dug, they hit a masterpiece. Instead of moving the artifacts to a distant museum, the city turned the stations themselves into underground galleries. At stations you can see ancient walls, clay pipes, and even graves preserved behind glass walls right next to the ticket machines. It’s essentially the world’s most functional archaeology museum. Id X.", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-25T18:00:21Z", "username": "Abhishek S", "text": "Shreedharan", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-25T18:00:23Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "Rome", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-25T18:00:30Z", "username": "Srijan Naayak", "text": "Greece", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-25T18:00:33Z", "username": "Vyomaa Patel", "text": "Athens", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-25T18:01:02Z", "username": "Khandoba", "text": "Great Q", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]